%S A401351 1,5,58,659,8072,78476,709598,6038941,50600865
%N A401351 Number of free polycubes with 2n cells that can be dissected into two congruent polycubes.
%C A401351 Each half is necessarily a polycube of size n. Here congruent means equal up to rotation, reflection and translation, so the two halves may be mirror images of each other.
%H A401351 John Mason, <a href="https://github.com/jmasonmilan/PolyUtil">Java programs to generate the sequence</a>
%H A401351 John Mason, <a href="/A401351/a401351.pdf">Bisectable polycubes of size 6</a>
%Y A401351 Cf. A038119, A399996, A401352.
%K A401351 nonn,more,new
%O A401351 1,2
